  // design: St. John's Memorial Hall pass (owner, 2026-11-23: "round all four corners of the hall, with the roof following"; docs/map-briefs/st_johns PLAN 4q). The end of a hall 16 m across, the hall on its south side: the side walls go on 4 m, then a quarter circle 4 m to the outer face round each cell's middle (in turned pieces, as the Round Corner's), then the straight end 8 m long; walls 0.5 m thick, the ground storey's `wall` (stone), the upper storey's `solid` (shingle), a band course (trim) outside at each storey's top, round the curves too. Openings as the Hall Bay's: a square one (sill 1.23 m) and a small one above (sill 5.93 m, the light of a Leaded Window at 5.7 m) in each side, two square ones and two wide ones (sill 5.97 m) in the end; glass and the open frames go in them. Floors: the ground, and the upper floor in rows inside the curve (the cells' outer corners are open ground). The Spiral Stair (16 steps of 0.25 m in one turn, its drum 6.5 m across) turned a quarter so both its doors face east, into the hall's middle; its drum 0.25 m off the west cell's middle towards the west wall, against the corner, the upper floor cut round it; no windows in the west side, and in the end two square ones at 3.2 and 6.4 m and one wide one at 5.75 m (clear of the drum). A roof goes on at 8 m (a Rounded Hip End, or a Rounded Spire over this end and the bay before it). Made by a script from these dimensions; the numbers are the data.
