  // design: Tileset 04, Tunnel Systems, step 1 (owner, 2026-11-13; docs/map-briefs/tunnels/PLAN_2026-11-13.md): the mouth of a buried tunnel, so no ground is carved by hand. North half: the vaulted passage under its cap, as the buried tunnel. A headwall 1 m thick and 4.75 m high (a metre over the cap, with a coping) across the cell, the arch through it (stepped masonry over the arch ring, which stands 0.12 m proud). South of it an apron between wing walls under coping slabs sloping from 3.75 m at the headwall to 1.3 m (one tilted box each, stepped masonry hidden under it). Its bore (map/groundBore.ts): the stretch behind the headwall cut out of the ground up to the cap and covered with earth (cover); the apron cut out at any height; rims: the ground along each wing wall goes to its sloping top, up or down, so no wall stands bare of its bank and no hill overhangs it, and the ground at the headwall comes down to its coping; an opening at its south edge: the ground in front comes down to the floor and the cutting runs on south until the ground as made is down to the floor (daylight), at most 48 m.
